# Deny everything, then allow exactly what the image build needs.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/

# The licence of the program the image conveys. Not documentation: the AGPL
# requires the text to travel with what it covers.
!LICENSE

# The one documentation file that is a distribution artifact rather than
# documentation: it ships in the image, for the operator who runs it.
!docs/legal/third-party-notices.md

# The browser application's sources and its lock file. Its build output is not
# copied in: it is produced by the Node stage, from these.
!web/package.json
!web/package-lock.json
!web/tsconfig.json
!web/vite.config.ts
!web/index.html
!web/src/

# The map label glyphs. They are generated once by scripts/generate_glyphs.py
# and committed, and Vite copies them into the build verbatim -- so a map draws
# its place names from this deployment rather than from a font service.
!web/public/

# Never ship caches, byte code or an installed dependency tree, even from an
# allowed directory. `npm ci` installs its own inside the build stage, and a
# host tree copied in would be somebody else's platform binaries.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
